# III. INTERNATIONAL HUMAN RIGHTS SUBMISSION

## *The Right to Epistemic Integrity*

### Proposed Addition to International Doctrine

*(Supplemental Protocol or UN Special Rapporteur Framework)*

---

### Article 1 — Right to Epistemic Integrity

Every person has the right to receive materially accurate information necessary for the exercise of free will, self-defense, and meaningful consent.

---

### Article 2 — Prohibition of Epistemic Violence

No state or institution shall intentionally distort or withhold material information in a manner that:

* Prevents informed consent
* Obstructs exit from coercive systems
* Undermines cognitive autonomy

---

### Article 3 — Right to Risk Awareness

Individuals have the right to be informed of risks to life, health, liberty, and environment arising from state or institutional action.

---

### Article 4 — Protection of Witnesses

Persons who disclose epistemic harm in good faith shall be protected under international law, regardless of classification or institutional secrecy claims.

---

### Article 5 — Archival Transparency

Institutions exercising moral, political, or spiritual authority must provide time-bound access to historical records that justify their legitimacy.

---

### Enforcement Mechanisms (Realistic, Not Idealistic)

* Special Rapporteur on Epistemic Harm
* Integration into existing ICC and UNHRC frameworks
* Use in asylum claims, whistleblower defenses, and sanctions assessments

